# Better Auth API Reference

## Sign Up (Email)
```ts
const { data, error } = await authClient.signUp.email({
    email,
    password, // min 8 characters by default
    name,
    image, // optional
    callbackURL: "/dashboard" // optional
}, {
    onRequest: (ctx) => { /* show loading */ },
    onSuccess: (ctx) => { /* redirect */ },
    onError: (ctx) => { alert(ctx.error.message); }
});
```
Users are "automatically signed in after they successfully sign up" unless `autoSignIn: false` is set.

## Sign In (Email)
```ts
const { data, error } = await authClient.signIn.email({
    email,
    password,
    callbackURL: "/dashboard", // optional
    rememberMe: false // defaults to true
}, {
    // callbacks
});
```

## Sign In (Social)
```ts
await authClient.signIn.social({
    provider: "github", // "google", "apple", etc.
    callbackURL: "/dashboard",
    errorCallbackURL: "/error",
    newUserCallbackURL: "/welcome",
    disableRedirect: true // optional
});
```

## Sign Out
```ts
await authClient.signOut({
    fetchOptions: {
        onSuccess: () => { router.push("/login"); }
    }
});
```

## Get Session (Client)
```ts
const { data: session, error } = await authClient.getSession();
// OR use hook
const { data: session, isPending, error, refetch } = authClient.useSession();
```

## Error Handling Shape
Errors are returned in the `error` object with a `message` property accessible via `ctx.error.message` in callbacks.

